# Code explanation docs

Applies to `docs/*.md` (the code-explanation series). Does **not** apply to `docs/plans/` or `todo.md`; those may stay notes-like.

`docs/event-debounce.md` is the style to match.

## Voice

Write full sentences and full explanations. A reader who was not in any prior chat must understand the page. Do not write as if taking notes for yourself.

Avoid: terse fragments, crib notes, bullet-only surveys, “v0 decision” tables with no surrounding prose, unexplained abbreviations, assumed context.

## Shape of a page

- Open with what this part does and which source files it covers.
- Explain why the code exists, name the types, and walk the real flow.
- Cross-links to sibling docs are fine; the page must still stand alone.
- End with what this does **not** cover, then a short summary in prose.

## Truth

Describe the program as it is written today. Do not present planned UX (from `todo.md` or `docs/plans/`) as if it were implemented. Link to a plan when future work is relevant.

One document per subsystem, not one file per `.rs`. Tiny helpers belong as a section of a parent doc. Action enums stay with the mode that runs them.
